  "proof": "Let A0,A1 be bounded positive normalized charged transfers with norm difference delta; no charged contraction assumed globally. Existing physical Pe band [L,U]=[exp(-a Emax),1]. Reference proof witness PI0 has strict interior spectral support and source tail paid separately. X=PE1 PI0, B=A1 on PE1, B0=A0 on PI0. BX-XB0=PE1(A1-A0)PI0. Resolvent intertwining integral gives norm(logB X-XlogB0)<=delta/L. sqrtB X-XsqrtB0 solves sqrtB Y+Y sqrtB0=BX-XB0, norm<=delta/(sqrtL+sqrtL0). Duhamel for unitary complex powers then norm(f_t(B)X-X f_t(B0))<=sqrtU |t/a|delta/L+delta/(sqrtL+sqrtL0), f_t(x)=sqrtx exp(i t/a logx). Add sqrtU0 times source-buffer projector leakage delta sqrt(dlow^-2+dup^-2) plus actual reference outlier tail. Same existing Pe/source/preparation; PI0 is proof only. Hilbert norm/bounded-effect estimate, not weighted Theta/L graph-domain control. Actual microscopic operatordelta, normalizer and source interior/tail remain uninstantiated."
